1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,045
Something's wrong with this shot.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:04,660
The crystal is fake... and it's sliding.

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:05,860
Now it isn't.

4
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:07,943
Same shot. Same crystal.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,590
The only thing that changed:

6
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:12,221
the software worked out where the camera was.

7
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,869
No measurements. Just pixels.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,388
This is matchmove.

9
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,840
First, tracking.

10
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:23,658
The software picks out sharp, high-contrast details...

11
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,060
and follows each one, frame by frame.

12
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:32,311
Every detail becomes a 2D path

13
00:00:32,351 --> 00:00:33,811
across the screen.

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,020
When the camera moves,

15
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:42,486
close objects sweep across the frame.

16
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,010
Distant ones barely shift.

17
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,981
That difference in speed... is depth.

18
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,683
But real lenses bend the image.

19
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,396
So before solving, the plate is undistorted.

20
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,337
Straight lines are straight again.

21
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,064
Skip this, and nothing lines up.

22
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:15,684
Now the solve.

23
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:18,313
The software guesses where every point

24
00:01:18,353 --> 00:01:20,630
is in 3D, and where the camera is.

25
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:24,355
It projects those guesses back onto the image...

26
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,022
measures how far off they land...

27
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,211
and nudges everything.

28
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:31,033
Again and again.

29
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:32,569
Until they sit right

30
00:01:32,609 --> 00:01:34,018
on top of the tracks.

31
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:42,538
The solve also finds the lens.

32
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:44,785
Try the wrong focal length,

33
00:01:44,825 --> 00:01:46,489
and the scene stretches.

34
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,514
The points drift off.

35
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,180
The real lens is the one

36
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:56,476
where the error bottoms out.

37
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,349
One catch: the solver doesn't know

38
00:02:02,389 --> 00:02:03,095
which way is up,

39
00:02:03,135 --> 00:02:05,020
or how big anything is.

40
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,372
So we tell it.

41
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:08,858
Pick the ground.

42
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:12,162
Give it one real measurement.

43
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:16,186
Now the camera lives in real-world space.

44
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,380
Position, rotation and lens,

45
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:22,187
for every single frame.

46
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,122
Render the crystal through this camera...

47
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,120
and it stops sliding.

48
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:29,677
It sticks.

49
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:37,100
Next time: rotoscoping. See you there.

